%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d7e76c79f1aa7df4391b0909e0ea0543, type: 3}
  m_Name: advisor
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: AssassinMystery::AssassinMystery.SuspectData
  id: advisor
  displayName: Lord Halvard Crane
  role: Royal Advisor
  profile: The Queen's oldest counsellor. Knows every royal plan before it is announced.
  coatColor: {r: 0.14901961, g: 0.21960784, b: 0.36862746, a: 1}
  accentColor: {r: 0.83137256, g: 0.6862745, b: 0.21568628, a: 1}
  skinColor: {r: 0.8509804, g: 0.69803923, b: 0.56078434, a: 1}
  headwear: 8
  heightScale: 1.02
  beard: 1
  greeting: Detective. The Captain told me she had sent for you. I pray this alarm
    proves to be nothing.
  topics:
  - question: What happens at the vesper bell?
    response: The midwinter toast. Her Majesty drinks the first cup from her own
      cask, as Aldmere queens always have. After it, she makes an announcement. I
      am not at liberty to say what.
    recordInNotebook: 1
    requiresClue: {fileID: 0}
    revealsClue: {fileID: 0}
  - question: What is the announcement?
    response: ...You will pry it out of someone. Very well. A full audit of the royal
      treasury, starting at dawn. The numbers have not added up for a year. I drafted
      the decree myself. Few people know.
    recordInNotebook: 1
    requiresClue: {fileID: 0}
    revealsClue: {fileID: 0}
  - question: Where were you this afternoon?
    response: Here in the Great Hall all day, arranging the seating and the speech.
      Mistress Agnes will tell you I was under her feet.
    recordInNotebook: 1
    requiresClue: {fileID: 0}
    revealsClue: {fileID: 0}
  - question: Do you know Lady Seraphine well?
    response: Barely. We have exchanged perhaps three words at court, and two of
      them were "good evening".
    recordInNotebook: 1
    requiresClue: {fileID: 0}
    revealsClue: {fileID: 0}
  - question: You pulled the guards off the cellar patrol.
    response: I did. The Captain's men were needed at the hall doors for the feast.
      The cellars hold barrels and turnips. Who would want barrels? ...Is that a
      problem?
    recordInNotebook: 1
    requiresClue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7e8bf38fb2664f3478c55f2f5a92c69e, type: 2}
    revealsClue: {fileID: 0}
  - question: Agnes saw you meeting Lady Seraphine in secret.
    response: ...Discreet woman, Agnes, until she isn't. Yes. Lady Seraphine wants
      her son married to the Queen's niece, and I have been negotiating terms. It
      is politics, detective, not murder. I would rather the court did not hear of
      it.
    recordInNotebook: 1
    requiresClue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a430af667ff8e1142b8996c52b0b6c52, type: 2}
    revealsClue: {fileID: 0}
